WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.263
Arithmetic lets us turn stored values into new
analytical measures Addition subtraction

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:12.224
multiplication and division are the most familiar
operators but Python also supports powers floor

00:00:12.237 --> 00:00:17.879
division and remainders In analytics the result of a
calculation

00:00:17.905 --> 00:00:23.356
is often more useful than the raw input Sales and
costs are useful but profit

00:00:23.382 --> 00:00:28.882
gives us another view of performance Profit divided
by sales can become a margin

00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:35.577
A current value compared with a previous value can
become a growth rate As

00:00:35.603 --> 00:00:41.330
you create derived metrics keep the units in mind
Dollars counts percentages

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:45.132
and rates have different meanings even when they are
all stored as numbers
